        "text": "<p><span><strong>Methods and interpretation</strong></span></p><p><span>Maintenance priority uses a rule-based score to group poles into High, Medium, Low, or Unknown categories.</span></p><p><span>Machine learning uses an unsupervised Principal Component Analysis (PCA) anomaly screen to identify poles with unusual combinations of asset attributes. It screened 11,126 poles and flagged 561 for review. Seven poles lacked age data and were excluded.</span></p><p><span>An ML flag indicates an unusual record that deserves inspection or data verification. It does not establish that a pole is damaged or likely to fail. Failure and inspection records would be needed to validate a predictive model.</span></p><p><span>The review list displays 25 flagged poles with the highest rule-based maintenance scores.</span></p>",
